e6" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8 & 5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry $c_{21}=3$ is to the left of the leading entry $c_{13}=1$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is **not** in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186619015 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b4a4a80-667d-52c6-80ea-2336cc6a2d56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618998} {:answer/id #uuid "768ded53-8b5e-5eb9-8ea3-44237ca267f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "768ded53-8b5e-5eb9-8ea3-44237ca267f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619008} :answer-field/id #uuid "32c08b9c-0c33-5ef9-840d-d2851889f349" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -9 & 9 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619000} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "143cfab3-99b7-5ce2-8138-1f32f1d7e780" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618993} {:answer/id #uuid "5b451a2a-3b55-5bd1-bea1-304af4d56a15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "143cfab3-99b7-5ce2-8138-1f32f1d7e780" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618993} :answer-field/id #uuid "387ce65e-280a-5b97-b6bb-0811e490cf8b" :answer-field/key "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619001} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b3820f-0dfe-5473-afac-87ca689c25a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618991} {:answer/id #uuid "31387c5d-1b0c-5862-8d9f-1224a36ed4c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10b3820f-0dfe-5473-afac-87ca689c25a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618991} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a3812c8-25f8-5971-98bd-1765f3a9d285" :answer-field/key "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 7 & -3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619007}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "95a955ac-07a2-541c-ab8b-4e62bab961a6" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry $a_{33}=-2$ is in the same column as the leading entry $a_{23}=6$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -9 & 9 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the first row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 7 & -3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry $c_{22}=1$ is to the left of the leading entry $c_{13}=5$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ are **not** in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186619025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f9e2b22-cc88-541c-ab5e-59cf84574f20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619019} {:answer/id #uuid "dc4ea06f-db9d-5e09-b7e7-1a73d864460a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc4ea06f-db9d-5e09-b7e7-1a73d864460a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619035} :answer-field/id #uuid "68db4034-e0d1-5973-8b79-67bb50d639da" :answer-field/key "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619006} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e8eaa15-99bb-5ea4-a28e-7d29ad7f2055" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619013} {:answer/id #uuid "d86492d6-617d-52d8-9b72-049a248db88c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d86492d6-617d-52d8-9b72-049a248db88c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619030} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8d70363-d26f-5dc0-8ac3-7955a2a48d4b" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619031} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b312096c-1102-50dc-942c-64a9ec7bf424" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619021} {:answer/id #uuid "c724beb4-fccb-50c8-93b5-fc61476dc528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c724beb4-fccb-50c8-93b5-fc61476dc528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619024} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbf016e9-7259-59eb-9997-e0fd93c8b245" :answer-field/key "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619034}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c7938343-412b-5fca-92c5-3a72b25b53aa" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry $a_{34}=-2$ is in the same column as the leading entry $a_{24}=-5$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are in row echelon form."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}]}
